<BaseLayout title="About" description="About APT Notes and its relationship to Hecavex."><article class="shell narrow prose"><p class="eyebrow">About the product</p><h1>APT Notes</h1><p class="lead">A curated collection of deeply sourced threat-actor dossiers.</p><p>APT Notes is a source-driven intelligence catalogue for searching, filtering and pivoting between selected threat actors, aliases, campaigns, malware, tools, targeting, techniques and attribution claims.</p><p>Depth is prioritised over directory size. APT Notes does not attempt to reproduce every actor record already available elsewhere. A profile is published only when HECAVEX can preserve source-specific attribution, meaningful operational context and an explicit review history.</p><p>It is a separate product from <a href="https://hecavex.com/en/">Hecavex Research ↗</a>, which remains the publication for long-form investigations, analysis and commentary.</p><h2>Coverage roadmap</h2><p>Coverage expands one dossier at a time. Priority is given to actors relevant to European and Baltic security, actors connected to current HECAVEX research, and records where public naming or attribution requires careful separation.</p><p>Published profiles are reviewed at least annually. After 180 days a record is marked review due; after 365 days it is marked stale until reassessed. A stale label describes review age, not actor inactivity.</p><h2>Machine-readable access</h2><p>Public actor metadata is available as version-neutral static JSON. Use the <a href="/api/actors.json">actor index</a> or the JSON link on an individual profile. These exports are research records, not a live blocklist or operational feed.</p><h2>What it is not</h2><p>APT Notes is not a live threat feed, detection service, SIEM, vulnerability scanner, authoritative attribution body or replacement for MITRE ATT&amp;CK.</p><h2>Editorial approach</h2><p>Source claims are separated from APT Notes assessments. Alias overlap is represented explicitly, uncertainty is retained, and corrections appear in the public change history.</p><p><a href="/about/methodology/">Read the complete methodology →</a></p></article></BaseLayout>
